<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/18th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · Battle</p><h1 class="enc-title">Battle of Halani</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1783">1783</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/18th-century">18th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Battle of Halani was fought in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sindh">Sindh</a> in 1783 between the Talpur <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/baloch">Baloch</a>, led by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mir-fateh-ali-khan-talpur">Mir Fateh Ali Khan Talpur</a>, and the last Kalhora ruler, Abdul Nabi. The Talpurs had turned against the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kalhora-dynasty">Kalhoras</a> after the murder of their leaders. Their victory ended Kalhora rule, and the Talpur mirs divided Sindh among branches at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hyderabad-sindh">Hyderabad</a>, Khairpur and Mirpur.</p></div>
